🔷 Software Engineering Methodologies (Techniques)

Software Engineering methodologies wo structured approaches hote hain jinke through hum software develop, manage aur maintain karte hain systematically.

👉 Simple line:

“Methodology defines HOW to develop software step-by-step.”

🔶 1. Waterfall Model (Traditional Method)
4
📌 Concept:

Linear sequential model hai — ek phase khatam tab next start.

📍 Phases:
Requirement Analysis
System Design
Implementation (Coding)
Testing
Deployment
Maintenance
✅ Advantages:
Simple aur easy samajhne me
Small projects ke liye best
Documentation strong hota hai
❌ Disadvantages:
Changes accept nahi karta easily
Late testing → bugs late milte hain
Real-world dynamic projects ke liye weak

👉 Use case: Government projects, fixed requirement systems

🔶 2. Agile Methodology (Modern Approach)
4
📌 Concept:

Software ko small-small iterations (sprints) me develop kiya jata hai.

📍 Key Features:
Iterative + Incremental
Continuous feedback
Customer involvement
📍 Agile Frameworks:
Scrum
Kanban
Extreme Programming
✅ Advantages:
Fast delivery
Flexible changes
Continuous testing
❌ Disadvantages:
Proper planning mushkil
Large teams me complexity

👉 Use case: Startups, product-based companies (Amazon-type)

🔶 3. V-Model (Verification & Validation)
4
📌 Concept:

Waterfall ka improved version — har development phase ka corresponding testing phase hota hai.

📍 Structure:

Left side → Development
Right side → Testing

📍 Mapping:
Requirement → Acceptance Testing
Design → System Testing
Coding → Unit Testing
✅ Advantages:
Early testing
High quality
❌ Disadvantages:
Flexible nahi
Cost high

👉 Use case: Banking, medical systems

🔶 4. Iterative Model
4
📌 Concept:

Software ko repeatedly improve karte hain iterations me.

📍 Flow:

Build → Test → Improve → Repeat

✅ Advantages:
Early partial product milta hai
Risk kam hota hai
❌ Disadvantages:
Planning difficult
Rework zyada hota hai

👉 Use case: Complex systems

🔶 5. Spiral Model (Risk-Based)
4
📌 Concept:

Iterative + Risk analysis combination

👉 Developed by Barry Boehm

📍 Phases:
Planning
Risk Analysis
Engineering
Evaluation
✅ Advantages:
Risk handling best
Large projects ke liye ideal
❌ Disadvantages:
Complex
Costly

👉 Use case: Large enterprise systems

🔶 6. DevOps (Modern Industry Standard)
4
📌 Concept:

Development + Operations = DevOps
Continuous integration & deployment

📍 Tools:
Git
Docker
Jenkins
Kubernetes
📍 Key Idea:

👉 “Build → Test → Release → Deploy → Monitor → Repeat”

✅ Advantages:
Fast deployment
Automation
Better collaboration
❌ Disadvantages:
Setup complex
Skilled team needed

👉 Use case: Big tech companies (Google, Netflix)

🔷 Comparison (Exam Gold ⭐)
Model	Flexibility	Risk	Use
Waterfall	Low	Low	Small projects
Agile	High	Medium	Startups
V-Model	Low	Low	Critical systems
Iterative	Medium	Medium	Complex apps
Spiral	High	High control	Large projects
DevOps	Very High	Medium	Industry
🔥 Final Conclusion (Exam Ready)

👉 Software engineering methodologies define structured ways to develop software efficiently.
👉 Traditional models (Waterfall, V-model) rigid hote hain.
👉 Modern models (Agile, DevOps) flexible aur fast hote hain.
👉 Project size, risk aur requirements ke basis par methodology choose ki jati hai.
